    </div>
  </div>
    <section class="about" aria-labelledby="about-h" data-rv>
      <div class="why">
        <svg class="jsal-mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect class="jsal-mark-tile" x=".5" y=".5" width="31" height="31" rx="6.5"/><path class="jsal-mark-j" d="M20 15V20a4.5 4.5 0 0 1-9 0"/><path class="jsal-mark-gem" d="M20 5l3 3-3 3-3-3z"/></svg>
        <div><h2 id="about-h">Why I made it</h2><p>I made jsal.ui to smooth out leveling, and it keeps going after you ding 60. It plans your trainer visits and talents on the way up, then your gear, dungeon runs, consumes and raid lockouts once you're there, with professions, guild crafting, a journal, daily games and a pal to look after along the way.</p></div>
      </div>
      <ul class="kit">
        <li><span class="i"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="3" width="6" height="6" rx="1.5"/><rect x="11" y="3" width="6" height="6" rx="1.5"/><rect x="3" y="11" width="6" height="6" rx="1.5"/><rect x="11" y="11" width="6" height="6" rx="1.5"/></svg></span><span><b>36 parts</b><small>each with its own toggle</small></span></li>
        <li><span class="i"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 6h12M4 10h12M4 14h8"/></svg></span><span><b>3 groups</b><small>Plan, Craft and Play</small></span></li>
        <li><span class="i"><svg viewBox="0 0 20 20" width="20" height="20" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 3l2 4.5 5 .7-3.6 3.4.9 4.9L10 14.2 5.7 16.5l.9-4.9L3 8.2l5-.7z"/></svg></span><span><b>Free</b><small>no subscription, code on GitHub</small></span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="band" aria-labelledby="release-h" data-rv>
      <div>
        <h2 id="release-h" class="sr-only">Latest release</h2>
        <p class="ver"><b>{RELEASE.version}</b><span class="tag">Latest</span></p>
        <p class="when">{released}</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul>{RELEASE.notes.map((n) => <li>{n}</li>)}</ul>
        <p class="more"><a href={UPDATES}>Every release's notes</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="band discord" aria-labelledby="discord-h" data-rv>
      <div>
        <h2 id="discord-h">Join the jsal.ui Discord</h2>
        <p>Bug reports, ideas and help, and the first word on what's coming.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="jsal-btn primary" href={DISCORD}>Join the Discord</a>
    </section>
    <section class="little" aria-labelledby="little-h" data-rv>
      <h2 id="little-h">And the little things</h2>
      <p>Smaller helpers around the game, each with its own toggle in Settings.</p>
      <dl>{LITTLE.map(([t, d]) => <div><dt>{t}</dt><dd>{d}</dd></div>)}</dl>
    </section>
    <section class="install" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-h" data-rv>
      <div>
        <h2 id="install-h">Install</h2>
        <p class="get-it"><a class="jsal-btn primary dl" href={RELEASES}>Download jsal.ui</a><span>Or get it from <a href={CURSEFORGE}>CurseForge</a> or <a href={WAGO}>Wago</a>, whose apps keep it up to date.</span></p>
        <ol>
          <li><a href={RELEASES}>Download jsal.ui</a> and unzip it into <code>World of Warcraft\_forever_\Interface\AddOns</code>, so you have an <code>AddOns\jsalUI</code> folder.</li>
          <li>Log in, or restart the game if it was running, then type <code>/jsal</code> or click the minimap button.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Every part has a toggle in <code>/jsal settings</code>, so turn off whatever you don't want. It works on its own, and plays nicely with <a href="https://www.curseforge.com/wow/addons/ellesmereui">EllesmereUI</a> if you run it. If you also run Auctionator, your profession leveling path, the shopping list and Crafting profit price things from its auction house scan (while Crafting profit is on, which it is by default); without it, prices come from your own auction house searches.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Is it really free?</h3>
        <p>Yes, all of it, with no subscription or Patreon tier. Its code is <a href={REPO}>on GitHub</a>.</p>
        <p>Made by John Salvador. Bugs, questions or ideas: <a href={DISCORD}>the Discord</a>, email <a href="mailto:dev@jsal.io">dev@jsal.io</a>, or use Report a problem inside the addon.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <p class="credit">Screenshots of World of Warcraft © Blizzard Entertainment. The pixel art of Jsal's Pals is jsal.ui's own.</p>
